WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00.490 --> 00:04.450
This morning, Aaliyah prepares for an upcoming video conference meeting.

2
00:05.030 --> 00:11.170
In this meeting, she will be sharing a change story with the department heads from across the entire organization.

3
00:11.970 --> 00:14.850
“David, hi. Do you have a couple of minutes?” “Of course.”

4
00:15.240 --> 00:18.240
“Let me guess. Is this about the video presentation?”

5
00:18.730 --> 00:22.630
“You know me too well, David. I have to admit I’m really worried about doing this on video.

6
00:23.080 --> 00:27.840
You know, I love presentations, but this video meeting — what if people simply tune out?

7
00:28.260 --> 00:31.750
You did an amazing job at the board meeting last week. Can you share some tips with me?”

8
00:32.170 --> 00:33.470
“Sure, I’m happy to.

9
00:33.990 --> 00:39.430
With something like a change story, it’s really important to think about your presence, especially if it’s virtual.

10
00:40.040 --> 00:42.910
You have a great voice, so you’re off to a good start.

11
00:43.370 --> 00:47.460
Is this usually where you take your video conference calls?” “Umm, yes it is.”

12
00:47.810 --> 00:53.700
“Okay, we have to find a better spot for you. You’ll need a well-lit room with a non-distracting background.”

13
00:54.120 --> 00:59.520
“You’re right, I get so distracted looking at other people’s backgrounds. But then I didn’t think about my own.”

14
01:00.290 --> 01:01.990
“Practice makes perfect, my friend.”

15
01:02.440 --> 01:05.600
“Virtual is such a pain. What else should I keep in mind?”

16
01:05.930 --> 01:15.810
“Honestly, one of the toughest things I had to get used to with virtual presentations was feeling like I was talking into a black box.”

17
01:16.360 --> 01:17.220
“So what do you do?”

18
01:17.960 --> 01:21.220
“I keep my energy high throughout my delivery and animate my voice.

19
01:21.570 --> 01:25.600
I pretend as though everyone is leaning forward with captivated interest in what I’m saying.

20
01:26.180 --> 01:29.440
I even dial up the emotion in my delivery in a virtual setting.”

21
01:30.090 --> 01:37.410
“What about other ways to engage the audience? I can’t just talk for 10 minutes straight.” “Well, there’s a lot you can do, depending on what fits the tone of your talk.

22
01:37.890 --> 01:40.550
You might share an image rather than a bunch of slides.

23
01:40.900 --> 01:44.960
You could ask a provocative question and get people to share responses in the chat box.”

24
01:46.630 --> 01:51.170
“Given that I’m sharing my change story, I could definitely think of some images that come to mind.

25
01:51.530 --> 01:54.530
Thanks, David. I’m feeling so much better now about the presentation.”

26
01:57.510 --> 02:04.450
“Hi everyone, thanks for making the time today. I’d like to start off with why now is the right time for MODA to change.”

